{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Until your return, etc.</b> The reason He gave two reasons — <b>for from it</b> etc., <b>for dust</b> etc. — is that the reason ״from it you were taken״ is not a sufficient reason to return to the earth, for behold, before he sinned he was likewise in this condition, and it was not decreed upon him to return to the place from which he was taken. Therefore He gave a second reason, saying ״for dust you are״ etc. The intention in this is that had he been saved from sin as reward for fulfilling the commandment of HaShem, HaShem would have strengthened within him the side of spirituality, and his body would have been purified, and the material would have been transformed and become form through the ascendancy of the spiritual part — whereas after he sinned, he caused two things: he greatly intensified the material part within him and concretized it, and the reversal into form was withheld from it; and also the light of the spiritual within him was darkened, and it had no power to illuminate the aspect of the material to make it form. And this is what He said by ״for״ — meaning, the reason that I say to you now that you shall return to the earth from which you were taken, and not before this, is <b>for dust you are</b> — meaning, you have placed yourself in the measure of dust, for you were concretized on account of your deeds, in that you did not keep the commandment through whose mediation would have come the purification; and since this is so, for every source yearns toward its source and will return to it, and the source of his body's mass is from the earth — from it was it taken. And the reason He said <b>and to dust shall you return</b> further intends to say that not only will he return to the earth, but his body will decay and it itself will become dust. And so they established the interpretation of the verse in tractate Shabbat (Shabbat 152a) in the story of those attendants of Rav Naḥman."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:03.156821451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}